  For every $\beta\in D_{\mathbb{A}}^{(1)}$, there exists $b\in D^\times$
  and $\nu\in D_{\mathbb{A}}^{(1)}$ such that $\beta=b\nu$ and $(\nu,\nu^{-1})\in C.$
